+# An Absent Link Parameter Is Passed to the View as an Empty Collection
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VETSSPECIALTYFILTER-001` keeps the specialty filter on every pagination link of the veterinarian list. The filter is unauthenticated caller text, so the rendered URL has to encode it.
+
+Thymeleaf 3.1.5 drops a link parameter whose value is an empty collection. It does not drop one whose value is null: `@{/vets.html(page=2, specialty=${specialty})}` renders `specialty=` for a null model attribute. An unfiltered page would then carry link URLs it does not carry today.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Concatenate the filter into the URL string**, as the owner list concatenates its page number through `__${...}__` preprocessing. Rejected: preprocessing bypasses the engine's URL encoding, and the value is caller text.
+2. **Duplicate every anchor**, one branch carrying the parameter and one without. Rejected: five links become ten, and the two branches drift apart under later edits.
+3. **Pass the filter as a zero-or-one element collection** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The controller puts the filter into the model as a collection — empty when no filter applies, one element otherwise. The template names it as an ordinary link parameter. The engine omits the parameter for the empty collection and encodes the value for the single-element one.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- An unfiltered page renders the link URLs it rendered before this requirement, so the no-filter path stays as it was.
+- The engine encodes the value, so a specialty name containing a space or an ampersand survives the round trip. Two controller tests pin the unfiltered shape and the encoded shape.
+- The wrapping is invisible in the template, and the model attribute carries a comment explaining it.
+- An on-page control for the filter, declined as `NG-10`, inherits the same mechanism.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VETSSPECIALTYFILTER-001
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § View Rendering](../system-design.md#view-rendering) — the rule this decision records
+- [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model) — the encoding this decision relies on
